{
  "id": "30256_tsukuru",
  "headword": "{創|つく}る",
  "reading": "つくる",
  "romaji": "tsukuru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to create; to originate; to bring into being",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to create; to originate; to found",
      "explanation": "To bring into existence something that did not exist before — a work of art, a company, a culture, a new future. A kanji variant of {作|つく}る chosen when the writer wants to stress originality rather than manufacture."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "30256_tsukuru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{新|あたら}しい{文化|ぶんか}を{創|つく}る。",
      "english": "To create a new culture.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30256_tsukuru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{祖父|そふ}がこの{会社|かいしゃ}を{創|つく}った。",
      "english": "My grandfather founded this company.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "30256_tsukuru_ex3",
      "japanese": "だれかが{決|き}めた{道|みち}を{歩|ある}くのではなく、{自分|じぶん}の{未来|みらい}は{自分|じぶん}で{創|つく}りたい。",
      "english": "Rather than walking a path someone else decided, I want to create my own future myself.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive; takes を. There is no separate intransitive partner — use できる or {生|う}まれる for the resulting state.\n\nORTHOGRAPHY:\nつくる has three common kanji, all read the same and all conjugating identically:\n- {作|つく}る: the default, for making things of any size\n- {造|つく}る: for building or brewing large or physical things — ships, houses, sake\n- {創|つく}る: for originating something new — a work, a company, an era\n{創|つく}る is outside the standard {常用漢字|じょうようかんじ} readings, so official documents and textbooks normally write {作|つく}る instead. It is common in slogans, mission statements, and company names.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {未来|みらい}を{創|つく}る: to create the future\n- {文化|ぶんか}を{創|つく}る: to create a culture\n- {会社|かいしゃ}を{創|つく}る: to found a company\n- {価値|かち}を{創|つく}る: to create value",
